generated_hash =

// @vibe/compiler/entry/source_compile/wasi_only — ADR-0070 / #897 compiler-
// internal contract, part of entry/'s own explicit "high risk" sub-batch
// (issue #897 body: "高リスク (要個別設計判断)... entry/ とそのサブディレ
// クトリ"), migrated alongside entry/compiler/, entry/compiler/fs_compile/,
// and entry/source_compile/ in the same batch. Its sibling
// entry/source_compile/gc_only/ (the wasm-gc-backend analogue) was already
// migrated in an earlier #897 batch -- see that package's index.vpkg for
// the simpler single-file shape this directory does NOT have.
//
// Directory-shared-scope package: 22 impl files (~1164 lines), of which
// only 13 carry a REAL exported def (`export fn`) -- the other 9 are pure
// re-export shims, each pairing a genuine `export ./sibling.vibe { name }`
// cross-file SReExport with a redundant bare `export { name }` block for
// the same name (harmless: check_contract's collect_reexported_names only
// looks at the SReExport form, so the trailing bare block is inert). The
// 13 real-def files, grouped below: linked_artifacts.vibe (4),
// linked_library.vibe (1), merge_sources.vibe (2), preprocess_compile.vibe
// (4), preprocess_interp.vibe (1), preprocess_interp_parse.vibe (1),
// preprocess_interp_rewrite_impl.vibe (1), preprocess_interp_string_build.vibe
// (1), preprocess_interp_string_collect.vibe (1),
// preprocess_interp_string_fold_core.vibe (1),
// preprocess_interp_string_fold_loop.vibe (1),
// preprocess_interp_string_fold_nonempty.vibe (1), preprocess_strip.vibe (1)
// -- 20 names total, all declared below.
//
// Deliberately NOT declared (the #847-documented trap this migration keeps
// hitting): path_utils.vibe's `empty_stmt_array` and linked_helpers.vibe's
// `path_to_module_name` / `resolve_reexport_chain` are each a PRIVATE local
// `fn` (no `export` on the fn itself) promoted to sibling-file visibility
// ONLY via a trailing bare `export { name }` block -- collect_impl_fn_defs
// sees them with `exported = false` (the SLet node's own flag, unaffected
// by a later bare SExport), so declaring them here would fail check_contract
// with "implemented but not exported by its implementation file" (the exact
// documented trap for the bare `export {}` promotion shape). Nothing outside
// this directory ever imported them by that name pre-migration either (only
// sibling files did, via directory-shared scope / leaf imports within the
// same directory, both still legal post-migration) -- confirmed via a
// repo-wide grep, not assumed. merge_sources.vibe's `collect_merged_stmts_recursive`
// is the same private+bare-exported shape and is likewise undeclared.
//
// Naming: no collision (wasi_only/wasi_only.vibe did not exist, mirroring
// gc_only/gc_only.vibe's sibling precedent), old index.vibe moved verbatim
// to wasi_only.vibe.
//
// External-caller fixes (literal leaf-path references into this directory
// from OUTSIDE it, now that enforce_incoming_boundary_fs rejects them once
// this directory is a package boundary):
//   - lib/@vibe/compiler/index.vibe: `./entry/source_compile/wasi_only/index.vibe
//     { compile_source_wasi_only, compile_source_wasi_only_rc }` -> bare
//     `./entry/source_compile/wasi_only { .. }` package form.
//   - tests/compiler_fs_test.vibe: had BOTH a leaf import of
//     linked_artifacts.vibe (`collect_linked_compile_inputs`) and an
//     existing package-form import in the same file -- merged into the one
//     package-form import.
//   - cli_adapter.vibe: two leaf imports (preprocess.vibe, merge_sources.vibe)
//     merged into one package-form import.
//   - cli_support.vibe: three leaf imports (linked_artifacts.vibe,
//     preprocess_interp.vibe, linked_library.vibe) merged into one
//     package-form import; the FOURTH leaf import (path_utils.vibe's
//     `empty_stmt_array`) is dropped entirely rather than routed through the
//     package form, since `empty_stmt_array` is one of the undeclared
//     private names above (see that trap note) -- its body is a one-line
//     forward to `@vibe/core`'s generic `array_empty[T]()`, already imported
//     in cli_support.vibe under its own name, so the two call sites just
//     call `array_empty()` directly instead.
//   - selfbuild_gate_sources_b.vibe: five string-literal fixtures embedding
//     `import ./entry/source_compile/wasi_only/index.vibe { .. }` as source
//     TEXT (compiled via the FS lane, not parsed as this file's own
//     imports) now target `./entry/source_compile/wasi_only/wasi_only.vibe`
//     -- the renamed leaf file -- keeping each fixture's original "leaf
//     import of an internal file" test shape intact (same fix codegen/'s
//     own batch made for its analogous `./codegen/index.vibe` fixtures).
//
// No import cycle found: none of this directory's own dependencies
// (checker/, codegen/wasi, codegen/common_base, core/, syntax/,
// module_graph_path.vibe -- all already vpkg or plain leaf files) import
// back into entry/source_compile/wasi_only/.
//
// Compiled into the compiler itself via compiler_sources_manifest.tsv
// (group `entry`): the old single `entry/source_compile/wasi_only/index.vibe`
// row becomes a dual row (this contract + wasi_only.vibe); the other 21
// sibling files already had their own rows and are unchanged.
//
// No exported types: Stmt/Expr (../../../core) and Token (../../../syntax)
// arrive as structural signature text (loader/runtime/core precedent -- no
// re-import needed here).

